Title: "Cheatsheet"
Id: "ac7712fc-0a1b-4e7a-8be7-66ed68156f54"

Text: "A compact map of the current language. Follow the chapter links for rules and
edge cases."
Id: "bb702f3d-ec0b-4fac-96a3-08620bf4b2ec"

SectionTitle: "Page And Structural Syntax"
Id: "dc6e57e6-0d51-4886-80bc-d0d11873903d"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
Title: \"A Page\"
SectionTitle: \"A Section\"
SubsectionTitle: \"A Subsection\"
Text: \"Markdown prose with $x \in X$.\"

[\command:of{A}]
Declares: X
when: A is \set
Documented:
. called: \"example on $A?$\"
```

The first section label chooses the group kind. Section spelling, capitalization,
and order are exact. Dot arguments are indented under their parent section.
Every top-level item has an `Id:`; `mlg check` generates a missing UUID."
Id: "1c53c2b2-bfaf-4864-90e6-6b212f54a8e1"

SectionTitle: "Commands, Builtins, And Expressions"
Id: "ab3d0515-66ee-458c-a33b-7fdffca760cc"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
\set
\function:on{A}:to{B}(x)
x \.set.union./ y
A \:subset:/ B
\(injective)::function:on{A}:to{B}
\set@{x_ : x_ is \real}
\naturals..succ(n)
\construction{A}#using{B := C}

x + y * z
f(x, y)
f[|x_ = 1, ... = 0|]
(x, y)
{x_ : x_ \"in\" A | x_ != 0}
(x_ is \real) => x_ + 1
(_ is \real) -> (_ is \real)
x satisfies (_ is \real)
```

Ordinary commands use one backslash. Builtin types and builtin commands use two.
The builtin types are `\\type`, `\\statement`, `\\expression`,
`\\specification`, and `\\anything`; `\\abstract` is instead a capability
target. The builtin commands are `\\not`, `\\and`, `\\allOf`, `\\or`,
`\\anyOf`, `\\oneOf`, `\\exists`, `\\existsUnique`, `\\forAll`/`\\forall`,
`\\if`, `\\have`, `\\let`, `\\piecewise`, `\\map`, `\\leftReduce`, and
`\\rightReduce`. Function values use `=>`; function types use `->`. Direct
components of `Defines:`/`Realizes:` commands use `..` in source."
Id: "038e0422-1849-4715-8276-b43fbf08253b"

SectionTitle: "Declarations And Definitions"
Id: "b04b5c8d-dcd0-44e7-a80c-7a493637a164"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
G ::= (X, *, e)        -- structural expansion
x := value             -- value binding
x = y                  -- mathematical equality
x is \set              -- establishes a type fact
x is? \set             -- predicate expression
G is \magma via (X, *)
```

`Declares:` introduces types/interfaces; `Defines:` introduces typed values;
`Realizes:` implements an abstract definition; `Refines:` introduces adjective
properties; `States:` introduces reusable propositions. A binding-position `:=`
introduces its left target, but right-side names must already be known. Defined
symbols cannot be introduced twice or shadowed."
Id: "c9cffbac-b39e-4fb6-98bc-4ec80f018015"

SectionTitle: "Definition-Like Groups"
Id: "e680919e-adb2-4f6a-94f6-c01da6c517e4"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
[\magma]
Declares: M ::= (X, *) is \set via X
specifies: * is \operation:on{X}
Documented:
. called: \"magma\"

[\naturals]
Defines: Nb ::= (N, 0, S(n_))
abstractly:
specifies:
. N is \set
. 0 \"in\" N
. S is \function:on{N}:to{N}

[\von.neumann.naturals]
Realizes: Nb := \naturals
specifies:
. N := \omega
. 0 := \empty.set
. S(n_) := n_ \union \set@{n_}
```

Common trailing order is `Requires:`, `Enables:`, `Documented:`,
`Justification:`, `Aliases:`, `Writing:`, `References:`, `Metadata:`, `Id:`.
`Declares:`, `Defines:`, `Realizes:`, and `States:` need `called:` or `written:`;
`Refines:` needs `adjective:`."
Id: "a6a2d152-2c25-4987-bd6f-d8e0068ec372"

SectionTitle: "Requires, Enables, And Aliases"
Id: "71f96a21-c676-43ae-b7a9-538fc682ec55"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
Requires:
. capability: x_ \"in\" X :-> x_ member_of X
. definition: \zero is \natural

Enables:
. capability: x_ \"in\" X :<->: x_ member_of X
. from: Y ::= {y__ : ...}
  capability: x_ \"in\" X :-> x_ member_of Y
. view:
  as: S := X is \set

Aliases:
. alias: f(x_) :=> x_ + x_
```

`:=>` is an expression alias, `:->` a one-way specification implication, and
`:<->:` a specification equivalence. Views justify requirements and ordinary
builds. The former hard-build and cast-relation syntax is removed."
Id: "f738f3aa-9224-4d11-b1f3-a1eb2fb71706"

SectionTitle: "Clauses And Builtin Clauses"
Id: "93fd5bdd-e376-467e-99fe-d087b887016c"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
forAll: x \"in\" X
where: P(x)
then: Q(x)

piecewise:
if: x < 0
then: y := -x
elseIf: x = 0
then: y := 0
else: y := x

have: P
iff: Q

have: P
asserting: Q
because: R

\\forAll{x \"in\" X}:where{P(x)}:then{Q(x)}
\\allOf{P; Q}
```

Clause bindings are local and may use refined types. Builtin clause arguments
are separated by semicolons. `allOf`, `anyOf`, `oneOf`, `not`, `exists`,
`existsUnique`, `forAll`/`forall`, `if`, `have`, `let`, and `piecewise` have
inline builtin forms."
Id: "2e364327-ac83-4e9d-945d-784b1b928f0e"

SectionTitle: "Rendering"
Id: "48e7a402-1ae7-4c57-be37-f8fcfd6d4ac7"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
Documented:
. called: \"function from $A?$ to $B?$\"
. written: \"A? \rightarrow B?\"

Writing:
. \"alpha :~> \alpha\"
```

Template placeholders support `A?`, parenthesis modifiers `A+?`/`A-?`,
conditional fragments such as `@[A]{...}`, and variadic join templates. For a
source parameter `n_`, either `n_?` or normalized `n?` substitutes the value."
Id: "d468fdf4-8a98-41a9-963f-b7eb2b19a53e"
